general_comments.body:
> Sorry but I don't really understand what you mean. Can you give a concrete example of the problem? Thanks

I mean that this is not platform independent:
> That's true, but your answer also worked for `$ NODE_OPTIONS=--trace-warnings npx jasmine --random=true --config="spec/support/jasmine-spec.json"`

Depending on your platform (Windows, Linux), the way to set an environment variable is different. The premise of node is to be as platform independent as possible, and this "just use a NODE_OPTIONS env variable instead of --node-options" just broke that, as you can't set NODE_OPTIONS the same way under Windows and Linux (and even cmd or powershell I think...).

Now, this old package.json file:
```json
{
    ...,
    "scripts": {
        "run-with-a-specific-option" : "npx my_command --node-options=--whatever"
    }
}
```
turns out to be
```json
{
    ...,
    "scripts": {
        "run-with-a-specific-option" : "NODE_OPTIONS=--whatever npx my_command"
    }
}
```
which doesn't work under Windows.

