review_comments.body:
@fritzy Yep, that is a possible setup, but the guard against rootNode will skip removing in that case (undefined rootNode).

```javascript
const rootNode = tree.root.children.get(depName)

// safely skip if either edge or rootNode doesn't exist yet
if (!edge || !rootNode) {
      continue
}
```

The issue is on subsequent installs where the root overrides aren't being reapplied like they are on the initial install - so if it wasn't a root dependency, the virtual tree that is loaded will be correct already. The issue is overrides weren't being reapplied when loading the virtual tree, so the workspaces were then installing their dependencies when those edges needed to be removed.

